                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{A}}(-,R(I))\simeq Hom_{\mathcal{B}}(L(-),I)
                    \\,.
          %h3#ExistenceOfEnoughInjectives Existence of enough injectives
          %p
            We discuss that in the presence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            at least, the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            has
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} enough injectives
            in that every module is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submodule"} submodule
            of an injective one. We first consider this for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InjectiveAbelianGroupIsDivisibleGroup"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baer%27s+criterion"} Baer's criterion
          #AbHasEnoughInjectives.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              has
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} enough injectives
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InjectiveAbelianGroupIsDivisibleGroup"}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              is an injective
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
              of a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible group
            %p
              To start with, notice that the group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              is divisible and hence the canonical embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{Q}
              shows that the additive group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              embeds into an injective
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              Now by the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
              every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              receives an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\oplus_{s \in S} \mathbb{Z}) \to A
              from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+group"} free
              abelian group, hence is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of copies of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A
              of a direct sum of copies of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mrow
                                %mi s
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi S
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    ker &amp;\stackrel{=}{\to}&amp; ker
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    (\oplus_{s \in S} \mathbb{Z}) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; (\oplus_{s \in S} \mathbb{Q})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; \tilde A
                    }
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde A
              is divisible because the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of divisible groups is again divisible, and also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
              of a divisible groups is again divisble. So this exhibits an embedding of any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              into a divisible abelian group, hence into an injective
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
