              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
              of this is a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde i \colon A \longrightarrow R(I)
            %p and so it is sufficient to show that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R(I)
                  is injective in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒜
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde i
                  is a monomorphism.
            %p
              The first point is the statement of lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RightAdjointsOfExactFunctorsPreserveInjectives"}
            %p
              For the second point, consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde i
              as part of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ker(\tilde i)\longrightarrow A \stackrel{\tilde i}{\longrightarrow} R(I)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is still exact
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L(ker(\tilde i)) \longrightarrow L(A) \stackrel{L(\tilde i)}{\longrightarrow} L(R(I))
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(\tilde i)
              is a monomorphism: this is because its composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(A) \stackrel{L(\tilde i)}{\longrightarrow} L(R(I)) \stackrel{\epsilon}{\longrightarrow} I
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              is (by the formula for
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(ker(\tilde i)) \to L(A)
              is the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
              this means that already
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\tilde i) \to A
              is zero, hence that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\tilde i) = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde i
              is a monomorphism.
          #RModHasEnoughInjectives.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              As soon as the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              has enough injectives, so does the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              over some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              In particular if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
              has enough injectives.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi AbGp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon R Mod \to AbGp
              has both a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_!
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              to
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_*
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coextension+of+scalars"}> coextension of scalars
              ). Since it has a left adjoint, it is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransferOfEnoughInjectivesAlongAdjunctions"}
              from prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AbHasEnoughInjectives"}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
              \=
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#injective_modules__abelian_groups
            Injective
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \mathbb{Z} Mod \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            be the abelian category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          #InjectiveAbelianGroupIsDivisibleGroup.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is injective as a
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/divisible+group"} divisible group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n G = G
          %p
            Using Baer’s criterion, prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BaerTheorem"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InjectiveAbelianGroupIsDivisibleGroup"}
              the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              are injective in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %p
              The group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              is injective in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              and generally that underlying any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              is injective. The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of any injective group by any other group is injective.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong Not
              injective in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              is for instance the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 1
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"}> projective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+presentation"} projective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+cover"} projective cover
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+resolution"} projective resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"}> injective object
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+presentation"} injective presentation
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+envelope"} injective envelope
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+resolution"} injective resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %strong injective module
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"}> free object
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolution"} free resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            %li
              %p
                flat object,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+resolution"} flat resolution
              %ul
                %li
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat module
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of injective module was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Baer
              R. Baer,
              %em Abelian groups that are direct summands of every containing abelian group
              , Bulletin AMS
              %strong 46
              no. 10 (1940) pp.800-806. (
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183503234"}> projecteuclid
              )
          %p
            (The dual notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+modules"} projective modules
            was considered explicitly only much later.)
          %p A general discussion can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+and+Sheaves"} Categories and Sheaves
          %p
            The general notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+objects"} injective objects
            is in section 9.5, the case of injective complexes in section 14.1.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Baer"} Baer’s criterion
            is discussed in many texts, for example
          %ul
            %li
              N. Jacobsen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Basic Algebra II
          %p See also
          %ul#Lam
            %li
              T.-Y. Lam,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures on modules and rings
          %p Section 4.2 of
          %ul#May
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
              ,
              %em Notes on Tor and Ext
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/MISC/TorExt.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            over the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+site"} etale site
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Milne"}> James Milne
              , section 8 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lectures+on+%C3%89tale+Cohomology"} Lectures on Étale Cohomology
          %p A study of injective modules in higher algebra:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liran+Shaul"}> Liran Shaul
              , Injective DG-modules over non-positive DG-rings
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.01479"} arxiv
